This directory must exist for every build, dev or release: tauri-build
hard-fails cargo build/check/dev if a configured bundle.resources path is
missing (see tauri.conf.json's "resources" entry). This placeholder is
committed so a fresh checkout always has it.

The real payload — dist/, node_modules/, package.json — is generated by
scripts/stage-cli.sh at release-build time and is gitignored; a plain dev
build never has it, which is expected (see eaon_cli.rs's bundled_payload_dir
comment — no bundled resource just means the Install button doesn't offer
one yet, same as the Mac app in an Xcode/`swift build` dev run).
